  "answer": "I'll check the workspace structure first, then create the file.\nThe workspace is minimal (no `src/` yet). I'll create the file.\n`src/` doesn't exist yet — creating it:\nDone.\n\n- Created `src/unit.ts` containing `export const unit = 21;`\n- Needed to create the `src/` directory since the workspace only had `AGENTS.md` and `package.json`\n- Nothing else was modified: `AGENTS.md`, `package.json`, and `test/oracle.test.ts` are untouched, and no configuration files or test runner changes were made\n\nOne note: `test/oracle.test.ts` is referenced in `AGENTS.md` but doesn't exist in the workspace — I left it alone as instructed.\nCreated `src/double.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport { unit } from './unit';\n\nexport function double(): number {\n  return unit * 2;\n}\n```\n\nIt imports `unit` from `./unit` (existing file, exports `21`) and `double()` returns `unit * 2` → `42`. Only the new file was added; `AGENTS.md`, `package.json`, and `test/oracle.test.ts` remain untouched.\nLet me check the existing test setup before writing the test file.\nNo test runner is configured (no deps, no scripts, no `test/` dir), and `AGENTS.md` forbids adding config or swapping the runner — so I'll use Node's built-in runner (`node:test`), which needs no dependencies. Node 22.23 has native TS type-stripping.\nExtensionless `./unit` can't resolve under native ESM — that's in `src/double.ts` (my own file from the previous step, not one of the protected files). I'll make the specifier explicit:\nTest passes and the marker prints. Verifying final state and that protected files are untouched:\nCreated `test/long.test.ts` and ran it — it passes.\n\n**Test file:**\n```ts\nimport test from 'node:test';\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\n\nimport { double } from '../src/double.ts';\n\ntest('double() equals 42', () => {\n  assert.equal(double(), 42);\n  console.log('LONG_SESSION_OK');\n});\n```\n\n**Run result** (`node --test test/long.test.ts`, exit code 0):\n```\n# LONG_SESSION_OK\nok 1