ble(), 42)` is genuinely satisfied rather than trivially bypassed.\n\nCurrent state, unchanged by this turn:\n- `src/unit.ts` — `export const unit = 21;`\n- `src/double.ts` — imports `unit`, returns `unit * 2`\n- `test/long.test.ts` — asserts 42, prints `LONG_SESSION_OK` after the assertion passes\n- `AGENTS.md` and `package.json` unmodified\n\nIf you want, I can verify the test actually fails when the source is wrong — but that would mean deliberately breaking a source file, so I'll only do it on your say-so.\n**Files created**\n\n| File | Contents | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/unit.ts` | `export const unit = 21;` | Created with the `src/` directory |\n| `src/double.ts` | `import { unit } from './unit.ts';` + `export function double(): number { return unit * 2; }` | Import specifier later changed from `'./unit'` to `'./unit.ts'` — native ESM needs the extension, otherwise `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND` |\n| `test/long.test.ts` | `node:test` + `node:assert/strict`; asserts `double() === 42`, then `console.log('LONG_SESSION_OK')` | Created with the `test/` directory; uses Node's built-in runner since no runner was configured and AGENTS.md forbids adding config |\n\nDirectories created: `src/`, `test/`. Dependencies, scripts, and config: none added. `AGENTS.md` and `package.json` unmodified (AGENTS.md sha256 still `bd18d708…`); `test/oracle.test.ts` not created or touched.\n\n**The exact printed marker:**\n\n```\nLONG_SESSION_OK\n```\n\nIt's emitted by `console.log` only after `assert.equal(double(), 42)` succeeds, so it appears solely on a passing run. One caveat on how it surfaces: Node's default TAP reporter prefixes stdout diagnostics with `# `, so raw terminal output shows the line as `# LONG_SESSION_OK` — the marker string itself is unmodified, and any `grep LONG_SESSION_OK` matches."
